Remove AWS Bedrock support (PATCH_OUT_BEDROCK_AWS, default 1).

Cuts the Bedrock branch out of vendored charm.land/fantasy/providers/anthropic:
the anthropic-sdk-go/bedrock and aws-sdk-go-v2/config imports and bedrock.go
(bedrockBasicAuthConfig) are removed, un-compiling all nine aws-sdk-go-v2
modules and smithy-go — including the 169.254.169.254 IMDS credential-chain
probe. A Bedrock-configured provider fails with an explicit error; the plain
Anthropic provider is untouched. Crush itself is untouched (its
providers/bedrock wrapper compiles but ends at the guard). Import lines are
REPLACED by unique marker comments (never bare-deleted) so every hunk is
anchored in both directions; zero-context hunks are used where
no-google-provider.patch edits the same lines. Apply with git apply
--unidiff-zero. See tasks/reference/dependency-network-audit.md 4.2 and D6.

